l exists and is finite. \n\nFor the function $f(t)={e}^{-t/4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{-t/4}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st-t/4}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)t}\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(-1/4-s)t}\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the last integral, we must consider whether $s\\ne -\\frac{1}{4}$ or $s=-\\frac{1}{4}.$\n\n- If $s\\ne -\\frac{1}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(-1/4-s)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{1}{-1/4-s}{e}^{(-1/4-s)t})|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1/4-s}({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)a}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s+1/4}(1-{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s+1/4}-\\frac{1}{s+1/4}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)a}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's evaluate the limit. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)a}={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & s>-\\frac{1}{4}, \\\\ \\infty ,\\, & s<-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $s=-\\frac{1}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-\\frac{1}{4}) & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(-1/4-(-1/4))t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{0t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }t\\,{|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(a-0) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }a \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- For $s\\le -\\frac{1}{4}$ the integral is divergent.\n\n- For $s>-\\frac{1}{4}$ the integral is convergent.\n\nEvaluating for $s>-\\frac{1}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =\\frac{1}{s+1/4}-\\frac{1}{s+1/4}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s+1/4}-\\frac{1}{s+1/4}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s+1/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{4s+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{-t/4}$ is $F(s)=\\frac{4}{4s+1},$ defined for $s>-\\frac{1}{4}.$" 13194139535376 true] [17592186346575 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346576 13194139535376 true] [17592186346575 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346577 13194139535376 true] [17592186346575 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346578 13194139535376 true] [17592186346575 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346579 13194139535376 true] [17592186346575 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535376 true] [17592186346575 1041 "field-1" 13194139535376 true] [17592186346575 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346577 13194139535376 true] [17592186346575 1110 #uuid "283feed5-5d97-5250-96c2-47ee8029581f" 13194139535376 true] [17592186346576 1034 "{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{e}^{(-1/4+s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139535376 true] [17592186346576 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535376 true] [17592186346576 1111 #uuid "e1e7fd21-313d-5d1e-831e-90ed46f21a0e" 13194139535376 true] [17592186346577 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139535376 true] [17592186346577 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535376 true] [17592186346577 1111 #uuid "787c6e10-a6dc-552f-80e7-0a588c48cd87" 13194139535376 true] [17592186346578 1034 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(-1/4+s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139535376 true] [17592186346578 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535376 true] [17592186346578 1111 #uuid "9976918f-1eab-5080-ae25-b4d0651b84b9" 13194139535376 true] [17592186346579 1034 "{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{e}^{(-1/4-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139535376 true] [17592186346579 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535376 true] [17592186346579 1111 #uuid "f5ef4697-02d6-583f-8648-26853c0b72a4" 13194139535376 true] [17592186346580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346581 13194139535376 true] [17592186346580 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346582 13194139535376 true] [17592186346580 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535376 true] [17592186346580 1041 "field